    "Bosch TT Water to Water"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Water-to-water heat pump controller",
  "applies_to": "Bosch water-to-water heat pumps fitted with the Control Air 5600 DDC controller running WWZ software.",
  "summary": "The Control Air 5600 also runs a water-to-water program (WWZ) for Bosch water-to-water heat pumps. Over BACnet MS/TP it exposes occupancy, control mode and source, Fahrenheit and Celsius setpoint pairs, load/leaving water temperatures, compressor and pump states and UPM safety alarms.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet MS/TP",
    "BACnet ARC156"
  ],
  "firmware": "WWZ.1.03",
  "default_device_instance": null,
  "access_inferred": false,
  "notes": [
    "Object names end in _1 as printed in the points list.",
    "Setpoints exist twice: AV 1-7 in °F and AV 501-507 in °C; temp_unit_mode_1 (AV 550) selects the unit system.",
    "BV 91000-91005 are factory end-of-line test points; do not write them in service.",
    "The PDF repeats row numbers 60-65 for the factory test points; all rows are kept."
  ],
  "source": {
    "title": "Bosch TT - Water to Water Network Integration Points List",
    "doc_number": "WWZ.1.03",
    "revision_date": null,
    "url": "https://www.bosch-homecomfort.com/us/media/country_pool/service/technical_guides/ipl_wwz_1_03.pdf"
  },
  "integration": {
    "summary": "Leave Control Source at BAS Occupancy Command, command occupancy with occupancy_cmd_1, pick the control mode (heat, cool, auto changeover or digital input) and write the occupied setpoints. Watch current_alarm_1 and alrm_status_1 plus the load and leaving water temperatures.",
    "minimum_points": [
      {
        "ref": "BV 1",
        "name": "occupancy_cmd_1",
        "why": "BAS occupied command"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 16",
        "name": "ctrl_source_1",
        "why": "Occupancy source; 2 = BAS occupancy command (default)"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 17",
        "name": "ctrl_mode_1",
        "why": "Off / heat / cool / auto changeover / digital input"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 4",
        "name": "occ_clg_stpt_1",
        "why": "Occupied cooling setpoint (°F)"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 2",
        "name": "occ_htg_stpt_1",
        "why": "Occupied heating setpoint (°F)"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 10",
        "name": "eff_load_tmp_f_1",
        "why": "Load water temperature"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 9",
        "name": "eff_lvg_wtr_tmp_1",
        "why": "Leaving water temperature"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 19",
        "name": "current_alarm_1",
        "why": "Active alarm code"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BV 20",
        "name": "alrm_status_1",
        "why": "Alarm present flag"
      }
    ],
    "enable": "Set ctrl_source_1 (AV 16) to 2 = BAS Occupancy Command (default) and write occupancy_cmd_1 (BV 1). ctrl_mode_1 (AV 17) defaults to 4 = digital input (off = heat, on = cool), so set it to heat, cool or auto changeover for network control.",
    "heartbeat": null,
    "remote_sensors": null,
    "setup": [
      "BACnet MS/TP runs on the EIA-485 port; the BAS Port Settings DIP switches select the protocol (BACnet MS/TP, N2, Modbus) and baud rate (9.6 to 76.8 kbps), the same for every controller on the trunk.",
      "The two rotary dials set the MAC address (tens and ones); the controller only reads them at power-up, so change them with power off.",
      "A Communication jumper selects EIA-485 (MS/TP, N2, Modbus, Lon) or BACnet over ARC156 at 156 kbps.",
      "Setpoints and configuration can also be changed locally with a BACview terminal or Virtual BACview."
    ],
    "gotchas": [
      "Default control mode follows a digital input; a BMS mode write does nothing useful until ctrl_mode_1 is changed.",
      "Use either the °F (AV 1-7) or °C (AV 501-507) setpoint set consistently with temp_unit_mode_1.",
      "Factory test BVs (91000-91005) force outputs; leave them alone."
    ]
  },
